etadata, check the codec list in ",[185,219,141],{"href":142},".",[169,222,224],{"id":223},"plot-is-blank-or-shows-only-fill-values","Plot is blank or shows only fill values",[165,226,227,229,230,210,233,236,237,239,240,243],{},[176,228,178],{}," — the colorbar bounds may sit outside your data range, or the variable uses a ",[194,231,232],{},"_FillValue",[194,234,235],{},"scale_factor"," that is not applied.\n",[176,238,182],{}," — reset the colorbar bounds (see ",[185,241,46],{"href":242},"\u002Fessentials\u002Fcolorbar","); check the variable attributes.",[169,245,247],{"id":246},"downloads-are-slow","Downloads are slow",[165,249,250,252,253,255,256,260],{},[176,251,178],{}," — chunks too small (per-request overhead) or too large (over-fetching).\n",[176,254,182],{}," — re-chunk to 1–10 MB aligned to your slice pattern; subset with the ",[185,257,259],{"href":258},"\u002Fessentials\u002Fvariable-selection","variable sliders"," before plotting.",[169,262,264],{"id":263},"the-tab-crashes-on-a-very-large-variable","The tab crashes on a very large variable",[165,266,267,269,270,272,273,277],{},[176,268,178],{}," — the browser tab runs out of memory.\n",[176,271,182],{}," — slice before plotting, enable ",[185,274,276],{"href":275},"\u002Fguides\u002Fperformance-mode","performance mode",", try a Chromium browser (often more forgiving).",[169,279,281],{"id":280},"analytics-webgpu-is-unavailable","Analytics (WebGPU) is unavailable",[165,283,284,286,287,289,290,220],{},[176,285,178],{}," — browser\u002FOS does not expose WebGPU, or no GPU is available (VM, remote desktop).\n",[176,288,182],{}," — use a recent Chrome\u002FEdge on native hardware; see ",[185,291,146],{"href":147},[169,293,295],{"id":294},"port-is-already-in-use-npmjulia-app","Port is already in use (npm\u002FJulia app)",[165,297,298,299,302,303,306,307,310],{},"Browzarr defaults to port ",[194,300,301],{},"3000"," and automatically picks the next free one. To pin a port: ",[194,304,305],{},"browzarr --port 